## Coding Standards

### TypeScript

- Use explicit types for all props, functions, and variables
- Prefer interfaces over types for object shapes
- Use proper type guards and narrowing
- Avoid `any` - use `unknown` if type is truly unknown
- **ALWAYS define types in the `types/` folder, never inline**
- Create separate type files for different domains (property.ts, user.ts, etc.)
- Re-export types from `types/index.ts` for easy imports

```typescript
// Good - Types in separate file
// types/navigation.ts
export interface NavigationItem {
  name: string;
  href: string;
  icon: React.ComponentType<{ className?: string }>;
}

// components/layout/header.tsx
import type { NavigationItem } from "@/types/navigation";
import { navigationItems } from "@/data/navigation";

export function Header() {
  return (
    <nav>
      {navigationItems.map((item) => (
        <Link key={item.href} href={item.href}>{item.name}</Link>
      ))}
    </nav>
  );
}

// Bad - Inline types and hardcoded data
export function Header() {
  const items = [
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "About", href: "/about" },
  ];
  return <nav>{/* ... */}</nav>;
}
```

### React Best Practices

- Use functional components with hooks
- Prefer Server Components (default in App Router)
- Only use "use client" when necessary (interactivity, hooks, browser APIs)
- Extract complex logic into custom hooks
- Keep components small and focused (single responsibility)

```typescript
// Server Component (default)
export default function Page() {
  return <div>Static content</div>
}

// Client Component (only when needed)
"use client"
export function InteractiveComponent() {
  const [state, setState] = useState()
  return <button onClick={() => setState(...)}>Click</button>
}
```

### Tailwind CSS

- Use Tailwind utility classes exclusively
- Group classes logically: layout → spacing → colors → typography → effects
- Use @apply only for complex repeated patterns
- Leverage Tailwind's responsive modifiers: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`
- Use dark mode classes: `dark:bg-gray-800`

```typescript
// Good
<div className="flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-lg shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">

// Avoid
<div style={{ display: 'flex', padding: '16px' }}>
```

### Component Structure

```typescript
"use client" // Only if needed

import { ComponentProps } from "react"
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"

// Types/Interfaces
interface ComponentProps {
  // ...
}

// Component
export function Component({ prop1, prop2 }: ComponentProps) {
  // Hooks at the top
  const [state, setState] = useState()

  // Event handlers
  const handleClick = () => {
    // ...
  }

  // Render
  return (
    <div className="...">
      {/* JSX */}
    </div>
  )
}
```

### File Naming

- Components: PascalCase → `PropertyCard.tsx`
- Utilities: camelCase → `formatPrice.ts`
- Pages: lowercase with hyphens → `saved-properties/page.tsx`
- Hooks: camelCase with "use" prefix → `useAuth.ts`
- Types: camelCase → `property.ts`, `user.ts`
- Data: camelCase → `navigation.ts`, `footer-links.ts`

