```

## Animations

### CRITICAL: Use Standardized Animation Components

- **NEVER** create custom animations or directly use framer-motion in new components
- **ALWAYS** use the standardized animation components from `@/components/animations`
- **ALWAYS** use `useSafeReducedMotion()` hook instead of framer-motion's `useReducedMotion()`
- All animation components are SSR-safe and handle reduced motion preferences automatically

### Available Animation Components

All animations are exported from `@/components/animations`:

```typescript
import {
  FadeIn,
  ScaleIn,
  ScrollAnimation,
  StaggerContainer,
  StaggerItem,
  AnimatedBackground,
  AnimatedBadge,
  AnimatedCard,
  AnimatedButtonWrapper,
  AnimatedGradientText,
  AnimatedIcon,
  AnimatedIconContainer,
  AnimatedStepBadge,
  AnimatedConnector,
  ScrollIndicator,
} from "@/components/animations";
```

### When to Use Which Animation

**FadeIn** - Simple fade-in animations for text, headings, or any content
```typescript
<FadeIn delay={0.3} direction="up" duration={0.8}>
  <h1>Title</h1>
</FadeIn>
```

**ScaleIn** - Scale animations for badges, pills, or small elements
```typescript
<ScaleIn delay={0.5} duration={0.4}>
  <Badge>Feature</Badge>
</ScaleIn>
```

**ScrollAnimation** - Scroll-triggered animations for sections
```typescript
<ScrollAnimation direction="up" delay={0.2}>
  <Card>Content</Card>
</ScrollAnimation>
```

**StaggerContainer + StaggerItem** - Staggered animations for lists or grids
```typescript
<StaggerContainer staggerDelay={0.1}>
  {items.map((item) => (
    <StaggerItem key={item.id} direction="up">
      <Card>{item.content}</Card>
    </StaggerItem>
  ))}
</StaggerContainer>
```

**AnimatedBackground** - Animated gradient backgrounds for hero sections
```typescript
<section className="relative">
  <AnimatedBackground />
  <div className="relative z-10">Content</div>
</section>
```

**AnimatedBadge** - Badges with icon animations
```typescript
<AnimatedBadge icon={Sparkles} delay={0.2}>
  AI-Powered
</AnimatedBadge>
```

**AnimatedCard** - Cards with hover and scroll animations
```typescript
<AnimatedCard hoverEffect delay={0.3}>
  <CardContent>Content</CardContent>
</AnimatedCard>
```

**AnimatedButtonWrapper** - Buttons with hover/tap animations
```typescript
<AnimatedButtonWrapper>
  <Button>Click Me</Button>
</AnimatedButtonWrapper>
```

**AnimatedGradientText** - Text with animated gradient
```typescript
<AnimatedGradientText as="h1">
  Animated Title
</AnimatedGradientText>
```

**ScrollIndicator** - Scroll down indicator for hero sections
```typescript
<section className="relative min-h-screen">
  <Content />
  <ScrollIndicator delay={1.2} />
</section>
```

### Reduced Motion Support

All animation components automatically respect user's reduced motion preferences. If you need to check reduced motion in a custom component:

```typescript
import { useSafeReducedMotion } from "@/components/animations/use-safe-reduced-motion";

function MyComponent() {
  const shouldReduceMotion = useSafeReducedMotion();
  
  // Use shouldReduceMotion to conditionally disable animations
  return (
    <motion.div
      animate={shouldReduceMotion ? undefined : { scale: 1.1 }}
    >
      Content
    </motion.div>
  );
}
```

### Animation Guidelines

```typescript
// ✅ Good - Using standardized components
import { FadeIn, AnimatedCard } from "@/components/animations";

export function FeatureSection() {
  return (
    <FadeIn delay={0.3}>
      <AnimatedCard hoverEffect>
        <FeatureContent />
      </AnimatedCard>
    </FadeIn>
  );
}

// ❌ Bad - Creating custom animations
import { motion } from "framer-motion";

export function FeatureSection() {
  return (
    <motion.div
      initial={{ opacity: 0 }}
      animate={{ opacity: 1 }}
      transition={{ duration: 0.5 }}
    >
      <FeatureContent />
    </motion.div>
  );
}

// ❌ Bad - Using framer-motion's useReducedMotion directly
import { useReducedMotion } from "framer-motion";

export function MyComponent() {
  const shouldReduceMotion = useReducedMotion(); // Causes SSR errors
  // ...
}
```

### Animation Props

Most animation components accept:
- `delay?: number` - Delay before animation starts (in seconds)
- `duration?: number` - Animation duration (in seconds)
- `direction?: "up" | "down" | "left" | "right"` - Animation direction
- `className?: string` - Additional CSS classes

### Important Notes

- All animation components are client components (marked with `"use client"`)
- Animations are automatically disabled for users with reduced motion preferences
- All animations are SSR-safe and won't cause hydration mismatches
- If you need a new animation pattern, add it to `components/animations/` for reuse
- Never import framer-motion directly in feature components - use the standardized animations

