## Data Organization

### CRITICAL: Never Hardcode Data or Links

- **NEVER** hardcode navigation links, footer links, social links, or any static data directly in components
- **ALWAYS** create separate data files in the `data/` folder
- **ALWAYS** define proper TypeScript types in the `types/` folder
- Import and use data from these files

### Data File Structure

**IMPORTANT: Use subfolders to organize data and types by domain/feature**

```typescript
// types/layout/navigation.ts
import type { LucideIcon } from "lucide-react";

export interface NavigationItem {
  name: string;
  href: string;
  icon: LucideIcon;
}
```

```typescript
// types/layout/index.ts
export type { NavigationItem } from "./navigation";
export type { FooterLink, FooterLinkSection, SocialLink } from "./footer";
```

```typescript
// data/layout/navigation.ts
import type { NavigationItem } from "@/types/layout/navigation";
import { Home, Search, User } from "lucide-react";

export const navigationItems: NavigationItem[] = [
  { name: "Home", href: "/", icon: Home },
  { name: "About", href: "/about", icon: Search },
  { name: "Dashboard", href: "/dashboard", icon: User },
];
```

```typescript
// components/layout/header.tsx
import { navigationItems } from "@/data/layout/navigation";

export function Header() {
  return (
    <nav>
      {navigationItems.map((item) => (
        <Link key={item.href} href={item.href}>
          <item.icon />
          {item.name}
        </Link>
      ))}
    </nav>
  );
}
```

### Examples of What to Extract (with subfolder organization)

- Navigation links → `data/layout/navigation.ts`
- Footer links → `data/layout/footer-links.ts`
- Social media links → `data/layout/social-links.ts`
- Feature lists → `data/features.ts` (or `data/home/features.ts`)
- Stats/metrics → `data/stats.ts` (or `data/home/stats.ts`)
- Mock properties → `data/property/mock-properties.ts`
- Form options → `data/forms/form-options.ts`
- API endpoints → `lib/constants.ts` (or `data/api/endpoints.ts`)

**Subfolder naming convention:**

- Use domain/feature names: `layout/`, `property/`, `user/`, `auth/`, `dashboard/`
- Keep related data/types together in the same subfolder
- Create `index.ts` in subfolders for convenient re-exports

### Type Definitions

- Create type files in `types/` subfolders organized by domain/feature
- Use subfolders: `types/layout/`, `types/property/`, `types/user/`, etc.
- Use descriptive names: `navigation.ts`, `footer.ts`, `property.ts`
- Create `index.ts` in each subfolder for re-exports
- Re-export from `types/index.ts` for convenience

```typescript
// types/layout/navigation.ts
export interface NavigationItem { ... }

// types/layout/index.ts
export type { NavigationItem } from "./navigation";
export type { FooterLink } from "./footer";

// types/index.ts
export type { NavigationItem, FooterLink } from "./layout";
export type { Property } from "./property";
```

## Common Patterns

### Loading States

```typescript
{isLoading ? (
  <div className="flex items-center justify-center p-8">
    <div className="animate-spin rounded-full h-8 w-8 border-b-2 border-primary" />
  </div>
) : (
  <Content />
)}
```

### Empty States

```typescript
{items.length === 0 ? (
  <div className="text-center py-12">
    <Icon className="mx-auto h-12 w-12 text-muted-foreground" />
    <h3 className="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold">No items found</h3>
    <p className="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Get started by...</p>
    <Button className="mt-4">Action</Button>
  </div>
) : (
  <ItemsList />
)}
```

### Responsive Grids

```typescript
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
  {items.map(item => <Card key={item.id} />)}
</div>
```

## Performance Considerations

- Use Next.js Image component for all images
- Implement lazy loading for lists
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Debounce search inputs
- Optimize re-renders with proper key props

## Accessibility

- Use semantic HTML elements
- Include ARIA labels for icon-only buttons
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Maintain proper heading hierarchy
- Add alt text for images
- Use proper contrast ratios

## Dark Mode

- All components must support both light and dark mode
- Use Tailwind's `dark:` prefix for dark mode styles
- Test in both modes before considering complete
- Use CSS variables from globals.css

```typescript
<div className="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
```

## When Generating Code

### Always

- Include proper TypeScript types (defined in `types/` folder)
- Extract static data to `data/` folder files
- Import types from `types/` folder, never define inline
- Import data from `data/` folder, never hardcode in components
- **Use standardized animation components from `@/components/animations`**
- **Use `useSafeReducedMotion()` hook for reduced motion checks**
- Make components responsive
- Support dark mode
- Use Shadcn UI components where available
- Follow the file structure above
- Add comments for complex logic
- Handle loading and error states
- Use semantic HTML
- Separate data, types, and component logic

### Never

- Use inline styles (use Tailwind)
- Modify files in `components/ui/` (extend instead)
- Use `any` type without justification
- **Hardcode links, navigation items, or static data in components** (use `data/` folder)
- **Define types inline in component files** (use `types/` folder)
- **Create custom animations or use framer-motion directly** (use standardized animation components)
- **Use framer-motion's `useReducedMotion()` hook directly** (use `useSafeReducedMotion()` instead)
- Hardcode values (use constants from `lib/constants.ts` or `data/` folder)
- Forget mobile responsiveness
- Skip error handling
- Create custom CSS files (use Tailwind)
- Mix data and component logic (separate concerns)

